      "text": "### Agaricus bisporus (Button/Cremini/Portobello)"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-EDIBLE-FUNGI.md#010",
      "path": [
        "04-EDIBLE-FUNGI.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mycology:04-edible-fungi, git-history:mycology:04-edible-fungi]",
        "canonical_path": "mycology/04-EDIBLE-FUNGI.md",
        "concepts": "[edible, fungi]",
        "current_path": "mycology/04-EDIBLE-FUNGI.md",
        "id": "maxim:mycology:edible-fungi",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mycology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[edible, fungi]",
        "section": "mycology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Edible Fungi",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nTHREE NAMES, ONE SPECIES:\n  Button mushroom: harvested young (closed veil)\n  Cremini (crimini, baby bella): brown strain, harvested young\n  Portobello: same brown strain, harvested mature (full cap expansion)"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-EDIBLE-FUNGI.md#011",
      "path": [
        "04-EDIBLE-FUNGI.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mycology:04-edible-fungi, git-history:mycology:04-edible-fungi]",
        "canonical_path": "mycology/04-EDIBLE-FUNGI.md",
        "concepts": "[edible, fungi]",
        "current_path": "mycology/04-EDIBLE-FUNGI.md",
        "id": "maxim:mycology:edible-fungi",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mycology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[edible, fungi]",
        "section": "mycology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Edible Fungi",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "CULTIVATION:\n  Substrate: composted straw + horse manure (Phase I composting)\n    → Phase II: pasteurization at 60°C, 8 hours (kills competitors)\n    → Spawn run: inoculate with mycelium; colonize substrate; ~14 days\n  Casing layer: peat + lime on surface → triggers fruiting\n  Fruiting: requires: high CO₂ during spawn run → CO₂ reduction → pin formation\n  Flush cycle: 1st flush (largest) → 2nd → 3rd; typically 4–6 flushes per crop\n  Growing environment: 16–18°C; 85–90% RH; CO₂-controlled"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-EDIBLE-FUNGI.md#012",
      "path": [
        "04-EDIBLE-FUNGI.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mycology:04-edible-fungi, git-history:mycology:04-edible-fungi]",
        "canonical_path": "mycology/04-EDIBLE-FUNGI.md",
        "concepts": "[edible, fungi]",
        "current_path": "mycology/04-EDIBLE-FUNGI.md",
        "id": "maxim:mycology:edible-fungi",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mycology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[edible, fungi]",
        "section": "mycology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Edible Fungi",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "COMMERCIAL SCALE:\n  Trays or shelf systems (Pascal's Law equivalent)\n  4–6 week growing cycle from spawn to harvest\n  Mechanized farms: Pennsylvania mushroom capital\n  Yields: 20–30 kg/m² per crop cycle"
    },
    {
      "id": "04-EDIBLE-FUNGI.md#013",
      "path": [
        "04-EDIBLE-FUNGI.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:mycology:04-edible-fungi, git-history:mycology:04-edible-fungi]",
        "canonical_path": "mycology/04-EDIBLE-FUNGI.md",
        "concepts": "[edible, fungi]",
        "current_path": "mycology/04-EDIBLE-FUNGI.md",
        "id": "maxim:mycology:edible-fungi",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "mycology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[edible, fungi]",
        "section": "mycology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Edible Fungi",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "WHITE vs. BROWN STRAINS:\n  White (commercial \"button\"): developed 1926 in Pennsylvania\n  Brown (cremini/portobello): likely the original wild type color\n  Same species, different maturity stage = different market products\n```"
    },
